      ],
      "message": "rpc: add background validation progress to getchainstates\n\ngetchainstates reports verificationprogress relative to the network tip for\nevery chainstate. A chainstate validating the chain underneath a snapshot\nstops at the snapshot base, so its value saturates below 1.0 and the\nchainstate disappears from the list before reaching it.\n\nExpose GetBackgroundVerificationProgress, which is relative to that target\nblock, as a separate optional field rather than changing the meaning of the\nexisting one.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Íñigo Aréjula Aísa",
        "email": "arejula27@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-09-09T19:05:00Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Íñigo Aréjula Aísa",
